title: Moscow's Money
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and congress = 0 and c_subsidy_timer <= 0
on-arrival: c_subsidy_timer = 5; month_actions += 1
frequency: 250
is-card: true
tags: international

= Moscow's Money

[? if comintern_member = 0 : An envoy of the Bolsheviks, travelling on false papers, has asked to see the Zentrale. Lenin's party wants a say in how the German revolution is made, and it can pay for the privilege. ?][? if comintern_member = 1 : The Executive's treasurer has come to Berlin with the accounts. ?][? if comintern_member = 1 and moscow_subsidy > 0 : Moscow already pays [+ moscow_subsidy +] funds a month for the papers, the full-time organisers and things the accounts do not name. ?][? if year >= 1921 and year <= 1922 and comintern_member = 1 : The money comes from a country where people are starving. ?]

- @more: Accept a regular subsidy.
- @once: Take one payment, and keep our own books.
- @refuse: Live on our own dues.
- @easy_discard

@more
subtitle: More funds every month, for as long as Moscow is pleased with us.
view-if: comintern_member = 1
choose-if: moscow_subsidy < 2
unavailable-subtitle: Moscow will not pay more than it does.
on-arrival: moscow_subsidy += 1; independence -= 10; lean_offensive += 1

The money will arrive every month through a bank in Stockholm. So will the letters from the Executive.

@once
subtitle: 2 funds now. The treasurer does not like our bookkeeping.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += 2;
Q.independence -= 3;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -3);
!}

We take the money and send back a receipt. We do not send the minutes.

@refuse
subtitle: [? if moscow_subsidy > 0 : Less money every month. ?] The Spartacists are proud of it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.moscow_subsidy > 0) {
    Q.moscow_subsidy -= 1;
    Q.independence += 8;
} else {
    Q.independence += 4;
}
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5;
!}

A party that cannot pay for its own paper, the Zentrale writes, will not make its own revolution.
